[{:db/id 17592186162018 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39a1a8bd-f69f-5f36-99bc-5bd95f9b782d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-39a1a8bd-f69f-5f36-99bc-5bd95f9b782d" :question/id #uuid "39a1a8bd-f69f-5f36-99bc-5bd95f9b782d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96238" :question/problem "$$\n{A}^{T}\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}73 & 24 \\\\ 24 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}{v}_{11} & {v}_{12} \\\\ {v}_{21} & {v}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the value of $|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|?$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ the columns of $V$ must be the right singular vectors of $A,$ i.e., the unit eigenvectors of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$ So, the first column of $V$ corresponds to the singular value ${\\sigma }_{1}=9.$\n\nHence, we need to find a unit eigenvector of ${A}^{T}\\,A$ that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=81.$ Computing ${A}^{T}\\,A-81I,$ we get\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,A-81I=[\\begin{aligned}73 & 24 \\\\ 24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-81[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 24 \\\\ 24 & -72\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-81I)v=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|=|\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}|+|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}|=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{10}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-01f21526-a5f6-5403-8d94-60d82378f21e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-01f21526-a5f6-5403-8d94-60d82378f21e" :answer-field/id #uuid "01f21526-a5f6-5403-8d94-60d82378f21e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7011776a-f74f-5038-88b7-bd75d4a9eff4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7450dd95-1930-5564-96d4-6c9e274f1579" "answer-089ec07a-5e86-5e2c-9ee0-7a59f0e9ce6e" "answer-da310c2d-2eb6-5830-855e-93aa19083cd7" "answer-7011776a-f74f-5038-88b7-bd75d4a9eff4" "answer-a9766852-3203-5031-bf4e-845ae1f644cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7450dd95-1930-5564-96d4-6c9e274f1579" :answer/id #uuid "7450dd95-1930-5564-96d4-6c9e274f1579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-089ec07a-5e86-5e2c-9ee0-7a59f0e9ce6e" :answer/id #uuid "089ec07a-5e86-5e2c-9ee0-7a59f0e9ce6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da310c2d-2eb6-5830-855e-93aa19083cd7" :answer/id #uuid "da310c2d-2eb6-5830-855e-93aa19083cd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7011776a-f74f-5038-88b7-bd75d4a9eff4" :answer/id #uuid "7011776a-f74f-5038-88b7-bd75d4a9eff4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9766852-3203-5031-bf4e-845ae1f644cc" :answer/id #uuid "a9766852-3203-5031-bf4e-845ae1f644cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-be1bd01d-d4e3-5a46-9543-53b198bb6268" :activity/id #uuid "be1bd01d-d4e3-5a46-9543-53b198bb6268" :activity/title "Singular Value Decomposition of 2x2 Matrices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050726 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-eb2350bf-19b6-5869-b8de-89f0f6ea18f9" "step-42130988-8a9c-5c98-b57a-c5c217558433" "step-b772e15d-